---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Grossline — what it does"
  description="How Grossline turns your Shopify, Google and Meta data into one monthly report an analyst stands behind."
  path="/what-it-does"
  wide
>
  <h1>What Grossline does</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    It pulls your commerce and advertising data into one place, computes the blended numbers that
    matter, and hands you a monthly report with the few findings worth acting on.
  </p>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <div class="cols">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>1 · Connect</h3>
      <p>Your Shopify store and your Google Ads and Meta ad accounts. Read-only — Grossline never writes to your store or your campaigns.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>2 · Blend</h3>
      <p>Orders, spend and costs land untouched, then become blended metrics: MER, contribution, blended CAC, payback — currency-aware, in your reporting timezone.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>3 · Report</h3>
      <p>A monthly PDF with the headline, the margin waterfall, the claim gap, what changed, and a short set of findings — reconciled against the platforms first.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>The numbers, done properly</h2>
  <div class="cols two">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Blended, not attributed</h3>
      <p>No pixel modelling, no attribution guesswork. Just what was sold and what it cost to sell it, across every channel at once.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Honest by construction</h3>
      <p>Money is integer minor units with its currency. Missing costs are shown as incomplete, never as zero. Every report carries when it was last synced and reconciled.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Findings, not dashboards</h2>
  <p>
    Each month you get a small, ranked set of findings — not a wall of charts. They fall into two
    kinds, and the report never blurs them:
  </p>
  <div class="cols two">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Where money is leaking</h3>
      <p>Efficiency below break-even, acquisition that doesn't pay back on the first order, discount share creeping up, spend pacing over target. Provable savings, ranked by the money at stake.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Where there is room to grow</h3>
      <p>When efficiency is healthy, where the freed budget could go — framed as a bounded test with a check next month, because a campaign at today's ROAS will not hold it on triple the budget.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="demo-note">
    Findings depend on the data a store connects; the report says plainly what it could and could not
    measure this month.
  </p>

  <p style="margin-top:2rem"><a class="btn" href="/free-report">Request your free first report</a></p>
</Base>
